Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Molecular Dynamics Notes", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9274462456303387`*^9, 
  3.9274462517019753`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cb127ea4-ca5e-4acc-bca5-\
cbdb6afa8a1f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Design of MD2 in ",
 StyleBox["Julia",
  FontSlant->"Plain"]
}], "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9750728260006332`*^9, 3.97507284169711*^9}, 
   3.975072881585597*^9},ExpressionUUID->"425bc38e-d77c-40be-ae86-\
0f3a951e38f1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Phil Shea", "Author",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.927446255686159*^9, 
  3.9274462606226816`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0a03cddd-2f34-4b3f-916b-\
4c8c6595259b"],

Cell["\<\
Derives the general parameters of the hexagonal array as a function of \
density, and shows how to create a nearly square box of particles. Calculates \
the angular momentum of an array and how to correct it. Develops techniques \
to deal with large numbers of particles, and includes a failed algorithm and \
one that works. Develops the Nelson Halperin order parameter (NHOP). Designs \
initialization of kinetic energy, and a few ways to initialize potential \
energy, resulting in an approximation of the PE field for a particle in the \
hexagonal array, and using the Boltzmann  distribution to place particles in \
that field. Examines the the radial distribution function of the array at \
zero temperature. Compares the Verlet particle propagation algorithm to the \
Velocity Verlet.  Computes Isobars and Isotherms, and examines the energy of \
dislocation (really point defects) under certain scenarios.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978008234431901*^9, 3.9780082836323957`*^9}, {
  3.993222649122573*^9, 3.993222660210786*^9}, {3.993981416346759*^9, 
  3.993981431914728*^9}, {3.993981551331912*^9, 3.993981583716464*^9}, {
  3.993981831423192*^9, 
  3.993982203563398*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8a133c63-92dc-4a85-9f0a-\
326b1f256db1"],

Cell["\<\
As of 25 July 2026, the notebook takes about 56s to evaluate.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978008234431901*^9, 3.9780082836323957`*^9}, {
  3.993222649122573*^9, 3.993222660210786*^9}, {3.993981416346759*^9, 
  3.993981431914728*^9}, {3.993981551331912*^9, 3.993981583716464*^9}, {
  3.993981831423192*^9, 
  3.99398185622331*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"50866e9e-bee8-412f-88f2-\
355c719eee42"]
}, Open  ]],

