  "Out[112]//MatrixForm=",ExpressionUUID->"ae65facc-4b68-49ea-8aad-\
6adb204d60a0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So some of the above violate the even number of rows rule (",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " = 18, 20, etc), and some are very close to square; the 16 x 18 is actually \
the worst.  If we have a number of particles we want to simulate, we can \
estimate the number of columns as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"2", 
     RowBox[{"N", "/", 
      SqrtBox["3"]}]}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "ebffafc0-f2ce-4512-9726-fe45a970be54"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977575858192171*^9, 3.977575931288829*^9}, {
  3.977575973297042*^9, 3.977575992617235*^9}, {3.977576025681519*^9, 
  3.9775760409613543`*^9}, {3.977576882567515*^9, 
  3.977576997736279*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3a16a5ac-3de8-4405-bbda-\
45001664d2b5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{"256", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox["3"], "/", "2"}]}]], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977577024192645*^9, 3.9775770495044813`*^9}, {
  3.9775777050935307`*^9, 3.977577714452343*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[113]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2c9c7ba5-f1f4-4f6f-b27e-47ea56907439"],

Cell[BoxData["14.889677745633593`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97757703987888*^9, 3.9775770514575768`*^9}, 
   3.9775777174707203`*^9, 3.9779993885154467`*^9, 3.978007322741315*^9, 
   3.97800803048482*^9, 3.978506482293024*^9, 3.990089330701248*^9, 
   3.993051959760556*^9, 3.993222249029173*^9, 3.9939811814390182`*^9, 
   3.994166422497867*^9, 3.9943236995966043`*^9, 3.994419614100273*^9, 
   3.9944367661698217`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[113]=",ExpressionUUID->"9b4d4602-830a-4c6f-afaf-f562e7f91d26"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
As can be seen from the table above, a row of 15 would yield 17 rows (which \
is disallowed) and 255 particles. So maybe we should do a ceiling operation \
on the computation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977577769211679*^9, 
  3.977577909189423*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b192a16e-83c1-44a8-8d4e-\
307bce27680e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 SuperscriptBox["1024", "2"]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.977577550107478*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[114]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ccbdcf89-8565-4ddb-a871-6a505ac38157"],

Cell[BoxData["1048576"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.97757755172219*^9, 3.977999388522788*^9, 
  3.9780073227822123`*^9, 3.978008030513063*^9, 3.978506482313147*^9, 
  3.990089330721611*^9, 3.993051959787455*^9, 3.9932222490698547`*^9, 
  3.993981181470894*^9, 3.994166422522769*^9, 3.994323699621488*^9, 
  3.994419614125847*^9, 3.9944367661965027`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[114]=",ExpressionUUID->"cb0daea2-809f-4040-9d53-46570f1537e2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And then we would have to search around that answer for a good number.  For \
example, to simulate a million (i.e., ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["1024", "2"], "=", "1048576"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "5bd3ac35-6d5c-49b0-b19d-3f5b88aa1af4"],
 "), we would compute:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977577060232498*^9, 3.977577135657048*^9}, {
  3.9775774816428747`*^9, 
  3.977577577059876*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ac77af49-a4f1-46f4-9759-\
e4c2bb1fb7a9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["1024", "2"], 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox["3"], "/", "2"}]}]], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977577499612958*^9, 3.9775775087472982`*^9}, {
  3.977577915365857*^9, 3.9775779507904167`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
