Cell[BoxData["\<\"test = {1/2, 1, 2, a79, 3, 3.4999, 7/2, 4, nnnd \[Alpha]79, \
tnnnd}\\n\\tThe explicit rationals are good test values whose results are \
easily done in your head (except for 7/2, which is the skin distance). \
\[Alpha]79 is the 1/\[Pi] density as exact number (\\!\\(\\*SqrtBox[\\(2  \
\[Pi]/\\*SqrtBox[\\(3\\)]\\)]\\)), a79 as floating point. 3.4999 is just \
inside the 3.5 skin value. nnnd is the next nearest neighbor distance in a79 \
units, and tnnnd is the third net nearest neighbor distance (i.e., \
2\[Cross]a79).\"\>"], "Print", "PrintUsage",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994436788612459*^9},
