Cell[TextData[{
 "We need to zoom into the contour plot to see what the potential looks like \
down there.  The plot below shows that the contours are basically circular \
out to at least ",
 StyleBox["PE",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " = 0.19.  The mean PE then can be achieved by using a circular Gaussian \
distribution whose standard deviation is the mean PE corresponding to the \
desired temperature.  We should be concerned that extreme deviations (3\
\[Sigma]) might extend into the less circular regions of the potential, but \
again the plot below shows that it does not."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967101793080943*^9, 3.967101854201782*^9}, {
   3.967101909371849*^9, 3.967101977482852*^9}, {3.9671020657636433`*^9, 
   3.967102285326384*^9}, 3.993131101029688*^9, {3.994169494223312*^9, 
   3.9941694974635773`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"570d4d8f-b776-4ef2-b474-\
849d065dd099"],

